---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ANALYTICS_TOOL } from '../lib/config';
const toolName = ANALYTICS_TOOL === 'plausible' ? 'Plausible' : ANALYTICS_TOOL === 'umami' ? 'Umami' : null;
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site counts, what it never collects, and who to ask.">
  <article class="wrap section prose">
    <p class="draft">Draft, not legally reviewed · v0.2 · 15 Oct 2026</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">No cookies. Nothing stored in your browser. {toolName ? 'Anonymous visit counts only.' : 'Nothing is counted yet.'}</p>

    <h2>What I count</h2>
    {toolName ? (
      <p>{toolName} counts visits and about 20 named clicks, such as "Resource Copy" or "Filter Used". It counts totals and never identifies you.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>No analytics tool is switched on, so nothing is counted. If that changes, it will be Plausible or Umami, and this page will say so first.</p>
    )}
    <p>Before anything is counted, the site strips the address down to its four utm_ tags, so click IDs added by social apps are never seen.</p>

    <h2>What I never collect</h2>
    <p>No cookies, local storage, fingerprinting, session replay, ad pixels or tag managers. What you type (search words, code words) never leaves your browser.</p>

    <h2>Other sites</h2>
    <p>GitHub data is fetched when the site is built, not by your browser. Links to other sites, including my tools' own sites, follow those sites' policies.</p>

    <h2>Questions or deletion</h2>
    <p>The site keeps no personal data, so there is usually nothing to delete. Ask anyway on the <a href="../contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  .draft { display: inline-block; background: var(--color-standin-bg); color: var(--color-standin-text); font-weight: 700; padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  h2 { font-size: var(--text-lg); margin-top: var(--space-8); }
</style>
